{"name":"Albino","hex":"#fbeee5","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"albino","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Congenitally lacking melanin pigmentation in the skin, eyes, and hair or feathers (or more rarely only in the eyes); born with albinism."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person or animal congenitally lacking melanin pigmentation in the skin, eyes, and hair or feathers (or more rarely only in the eyes); one born with albinism."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/albino"}],"entries":[{"title":"Albinism","blocks":[{"text":"Albinism is the congenital absence of pigmentation in an animal or plant resulting in \"hair being white, red, or yellow\", \"feathers, scales, and skin being yellow\", \"eyes being red, pink, purple, violet, or blue\", and \"leaves or stems being white or yellow\", if applicable. Individuals with the condition are referred to as albinos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Albino_Alligator_2008.jpg/330px-Albino_Alligator_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albinism"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Alligator_mississippiensis_%282%29%2C.jpg/500px-Alligator_mississippiensis_%282%29%2C.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Alligator_mississippiensis_%282%29%2C.jpg/1280px-Alligator_mississippiensis_%282%29%2C.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Alligator_mississippiensis_%282%29%2C.jpg/500px-Alligator_mississippiensis_%282%29%2C.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlligator_mississippiensis_(2)%2C.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wi